Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Report Builder: fix crash, corrupt exports, blank
 exhibits, add attribution

P0/P1 fixes for the build-your-own-report tool:
- Crash: declare isAiChat/isExhibit and import ReactMarkdown (both were used
  but undeclared, white-screening any report containing an AI answer). Add an
  unknown-type fallback and wrap every block in an error boundary so one bad
  item can take down the whole report.
- Exports: replace literal double-backslash newlines with real newlines in the
  CSV and Text exports (both previously emitted a single unreadable line).
- Exhibits: render exhibit items (factor_grid, correlation_matrix) as a titled
  summary block with their captured parameters and a link to the interactive
  version, instead of a blank block; include them in the Text export.
- Image export: filter out .no-print editing chrome (move/remove arrows, add
  buttons) so it is not baked into the PNG.
- Attribution: add a self-citing footer (source, URL, self-selection caveat,
  date) inside the captured node so PNG and PDF exports carry provenance.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01R5KRGTuQddQkUdyoTpsKih
